children in whom was no blemish, but well favoured, and skilful in all wisdom, and cunning in knowledge, and understanding science, and such as had ability in them to stand in the king's palace, and whom they might teach the learning and the tongue of the Chaldeans.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ»And the king appointed them a daily provision of the king's meat, and of the wine which he drank: so nourishing them three years, that at the end thereof they might stand before the king.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVNow among these were of the children of Judah, Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¹unto whom the prince of the eunuchs gave names: for he gave unto Daniel the name of Belteshazzar; and to Hananiah, of Shadrach; and to Mishael, of Meshach; and to Azariah, of Abed-nego.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse
¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŞBut Daniel purposed in his heart that he would not defile himself with the portion of the king's meat, nor with the wine which he drank: therefore he requested of the prince of the eunuchs that he might not defile himself.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVNow God had brought Daniel into favour and tender love with the prince of the eunuchs.¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚAnd the prince of the eunuchs said unto Daniel, I fear my lord the king, who hath appointed your meat and your drink: for why should he see your faces worse liking than the children which are of your sort? then shall ye make me endanger my head to the king.¦layout ªlast_verse
…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙoThen said Daniel to Melzar, whom the prince of the eunuchs had set over Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdProve thy servants, I beseech thee, ten days; and let them give us pulse to eat, and water to drink.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ°Then let our countenances be looked upon before thee, and the countenance of the children that eat of the portion of the king's meat: and as thou seest, deal with thy servants.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙASo he consented to them in this matter, and proved them ten days.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ•And at the end of ten days their countenances appeared fairer and fatter in flesh than all the children which did eat the portion of the king's meat.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjThus Melzar took away the portion of their meat, and the wine that they should drink; and gave them pulse.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‘As for these four children, God gave them knowledge and skill in all learning and wisdom: and Daniel had understanding in all visions and dreams.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNow at the end of the days that the king had said he should bring them in, then the prince of the eunuchs brought them in before Nebuchadnezzar.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ•And the king communed with them; and among them all was found none like Daniel, Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah: therefore stood they before the king.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ±And in all matters of wisdom and understanding, that the king enquired of them,